                "entry_id": "ff130a18-cb6f-3d8e-900a-c863a543a146",
                "word": "solanine",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "557c0338-a1a3-45ce-a932-f0cbcc27eb0b",
                        "entry_id": "ff130a18-cb6f-3d8e-900a-c863a543a146",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "solanines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5bb7f68c-f0e2-330c-adb3-2a6a3efab731",
                        "entry_id": "ff130a18-cb6f-3d8e-900a-c863a543a146",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A poisonous glycoalkaloid found in many species of the nightshade family Solanaceae, including potato and tomato."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6e4fb52-f905-4e55-8e97-8453d57f349b",
                                "sense_id": "5bb7f68c-f0e2-330c-adb3-2a6a3efab731",
                                "text": "1989, R. P. Sharma, D. K. Salunkhe, Chapter 8: Solanum Glycoalkaloids, Peter R. Cheeke (editor), Toxicants of Plant Origin: Alkaloids, Volume 1: Alkaloids, page 214,\nApparently the high activity of α-solanine injected into the bloodstream may be due to cholinesterase inhibition, while the lesser effects of orally administered α-solanine could reflect its poor adsorption from the gastrointestinal tract."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c3babb2-b990-4d07-9573-d7a7f2b9a5e9",
                                "sense_id": "5bb7f68c-f0e2-330c-adb3-2a6a3efab731",
                                "text": "The most potent inhibitors are found in potatoes, and of these the most active component is the glycoalkaloid solanine.\nThe toxicity of solanine has been the subject of extensive study."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6843a538-7951-41e6-9da2-efe986cb229e",
                                "sense_id": "5bb7f68c-f0e2-330c-adb3-2a6a3efab731",
                                "text": "Evidently, during the ripening process, the solanines are metabolised to neutral saponins without the occurrence of glycoside hydrolysis."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3109f0f8-ef9e-4d57-871e-f88b26c36068",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff130a18-cb6f-3d8e-900a-c863a543a146",
                        "source_sense_id": "5bb7f68c-f0e2-330c-adb3-2a6a3efab731",
                        "source_sense_description": "poisonous glycoalkaloid found in many species of nightshade",
                        "target_lang_word": "solanine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "solanine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14828b36-69e5-32ab-ae02-bc448dc9836b",
                                        "entry_id": "eedb0484-f475-3b37-a260-c6670715a0f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alcaloïde de la famille des glycoalcaloïdes, toxique, extrait des baies de la morelle noire, des tiges de la douce-amère, des germes de la pomme de terre. Toutes les solanacées en contiennent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7da7926-0b34-4cc6-958d-63c90e771067",
                                                "sense_id": "14828b36-69e5-32ab-ae02-bc448dc9836b",
                                                "text": "Autour des asperges, côté sud, pour que le soleil soit bien présent, placez des tomates. Les criocères sont friands de l'asperge, mais détestent la solanine contenue dans les tomates."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
